## 2. Choose the right test

| Test | What it checks | Chicken-order example |
|---|---|---|
| Unit | One behavior with controlled dependencies. | Invalid quantity makes no submission call. |
| Integration | Components working together. | The repository result updates the Redux Toolkit store or ViewModel correctly. |
| Component / UI | User actions and visible state. | Submitting shows progress, followed by the returned confirmation. |
| Native device | The installed app on a selected device and OS. | An approved test account completes the order journey in an isolated environment. |
| Coverage check | Which production code the tests executed. | Every required production file is accounted for and supported metrics reach 100%. |

**100% production-code coverage is required within the defined scope and supported metrics.** Coverage does not prove assertions are correct or replace device tests, code review, or security assessment.

| Application | Local logic tests | Native device tests |
|---|---|---|
| Android | Existing JUnit setup. | JUnit instrumentation with AndroidJUnitRunner and the configured UI-test framework. |
| iOS | Existing XCTest / approved Swift Testing setup. | XCUITest with matching application and test-runner packages. |
| React Native | Existing Jest setup for JavaScript/TypeScript, including Redux Toolkit behavior. | Android: the team's JUnit instrumentation path. iOS: the separately configured XCUITest path where approved. |

JUnit XML is a report format. Exporting Jest results as JUnit XML does not run Android instrumentation tests. Android JUnit does not execute the iOS suite.

