## 4. Connect the results to CI/CD

| Check | Responsibility | Result to inspect |
|---|---|---|
| PR review | Danger and required repository checks. | Feedback and required statuses for the reviewed revision. Danger is not the feature-test runner. |
| Tests and coverage | Configured Bitrise workflows and repository scripts. | Completed suites, fresh reports, full production scope, and passing thresholds. |
| Parallel execution | Approved module selection and workflow handoff. | Required selected jobs actually ran; shared changes and missing flags are handled correctly. |
| Real devices | Bitrise prepares packages and invokes the Sauce Labs integration. | Matching app/test packages, completed run identity, actual device/OS, and suite outcome. |
| Binary security | NowSecure assessment and severity gate. | Completed assessment and the configured release decision. A test pass does not satisfy this gate. |
| Delivery | Protected signing and destination-specific workflows. | Exact-version distribution and user visibility. A device-test pass alone is not a release. |

The supplied Sauce Labs integration uses `.sauce/saucelabs_request.yml` with the input `saucelabs_request_yml`. Its complete private schema must come from the pinned step's owner. Keep the exact workflow YAML, input mappings, and packaging instructions in [Sauce Labs Device Testing](/mobile/testing-quality/sauce-labs-real-device-testing/); this overview does not introduce a second configuration.

Use [Bitrise Pipelines](/mobile/cicd/bitrise-pipelines/), [Parallel Testing](/mobile/cicd/parallel-testing/), and [NowSecure Security Gates](/mobile/cicd/nowsecure-security-gates/) for their respective integration details. Keep existing enrollment for later builds; test changes do not require creating another Bitrise app.

## 5. Read the outcome correctly

| Observed result | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Build completed | Compilation succeeded; inspect whether tests ran. |
| Coverage report exists | Validate scope and thresholds before claiming coverage passed. |
| Packages uploaded or test job created | Device execution is not yet confirmed. |
| Required suites completed successfully | Check source/artifact association, test counts, and every required device result. |
| Required result failed, missing, or unknown | Investigate; do not report a pass. |

Use independent synthetic data for parallel order tests. Keep runtime credentials in the approved injection mechanism. If a cloud write has an uncertain result, preserve evidence and follow the CI/CD reconciliation procedure before another write.

