## 5. Verify that the draft detects the intended regression

Review the generated diff before execution. Reject invented imports, unused tests, changed production requirements, no-op assertions, fixed sleeps, hidden retries, and coverage exclusions.

| Verification | What to observe |
| :--- | :--- |
| Correct implementation | Test passes with the expected assertions and call counts. |
| Controlled local regression | The relevant test fails for the intended reason. |
| Failure/unknown outcome | No fabricated confirmation or automatic repeat of an uncertain order. |
| Complete coverage gate | Full production inventory and thresholds remain enforced. |

To demonstrate regression detection, use an isolated local test branch/fixture. For example, temporarily introduce an incorrect quote in the sample or remove the sample's confirmed-state guard, then run the relevant test. Confirm the intended assertion fails; restore the change in the editor and rerun. Never commit/deploy the deliberately broken implementation or weaken the expected result to make it green.

